Chapter: ValueEq

 Stage 2 of the proof system: value-level propositional equality with
 SYNTACTIC checking (no normalizer yet). Terms are names, applications,
 and constructor applications, represented via TypeCon/TypeApply/TypeVar
 and compared structurally by the PropEqTy unifier arm. Reflexive value
 equalities check and erase; the negative cases live in
 codex/test/errors/term-mismatch.

Section: Terms

  reverse : List a -> List a
  reverse (xs) = xs

  claim refl-var : xs === xs
  proof refl-var = Refl
  qed

  claim refl-app : reverse xs === reverse xs
  proof refl-app = Refl
  qed

  claim refl-ctor : Cons h t === Cons h t
  proof refl-ctor = Refl
  qed

  claim refl-nest : reverse (reverse xs) === reverse (reverse xs)
  proof refl-nest = Refl
  qed

  claim sym-app : reverse xs === reverse xs
  proof sym-app = sym Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "value-eq ok"
  end
